From dccc20c92474b74302e5f135ec6ddc972a15b03a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:01:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mbaa: fix census extents for unsorted tables, policy silent
 no-ops

tools/mbaa-texture-census.js
  * A member's extent is the distance to the next member IN THE FILE, not to
    the next entry in the name table. Reading the successor out of the table
    gave end === start (length 0, never classified, never pinned) for any
    member whose table neighbour sat earlier in the file, while the member
    before it swallowed every byte between them -- so a texture silently
    streamed instead of being pinned, which is the exact failure the tool
    exists to remove, and it failed with no message. Extents now come from the
    sorted offset list; table order is kept so names still pair.

lib/app-files.js
  * An unsized preloadAssets name was emitted as {loadMode:'required',
    size:null}; host.js rejects that at launch ('Invalid manifest size'), so a
    typo or a missing size turned a slow launch into no launch. It is now left
    as it was, reported in summary.preloadSkipped and warned about.
  * A preloadRanges key was matched case-sensitively against the URL leaf, so
    {'0002.P': ...} silently matched nothing and the archive fell back to a
    whole-file preload -- a 900MB launch from a table that looks right. Keys
    now resolve exactly as preloadAssets names do (exact, URL, case-insensitive
    leaf); a list measured on other bytes is refused AND reported; a table no
    file consulted is called out by name instead of vanishing.

Tests: test-mbaa-texture-census.js (unsorted table), test-app-files-switches.js
(unsized preload, key spellings, size mismatch, unused table).

Verified: build.sh 1765269 bytes, region hash c4c5e06a29d651ae, 1837 test
files, silent-stub inventory pinned, nine related tests PASS.
